      en: "The Gudenieki Rise in western Latvia is a 75-meter-high terminal moraine ridge stretching 9 kilometers. Geologically, it consists of gravels and sands deposited during the ice age. The summits are covered by coniferous forests, while the valleys are used for agriculture. The rise serves as an important drinking water resource for surrounding communities. Several bogs in the area act as carbon sinks. Agriculture focuses on oat and potato cultivation. The Gudenieki Rise is part of the Natura 2000 site 'Gudenieki'.",
